  ('breckenridge-colorado', '12A', 'Breckenridge', 'United States', 'A Victorian gold-rush town under the highest chairlift in', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'The Colorado Rockies', '{"adventure","culinary","entertainment","expedition","family","romance","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Breckenridge Ski Resort = Vail Resorts / Epic; five peaks (6,7,8,9,10), ~2,908 skiable acres, 187 trails, terrain parks ~25 ac; difficulty 14% beg / 31% int / 19% adv / 36% expert, ~40% above treeline","Imperial Express SuperChair = highest chairlift in North America at 12,840 ft (installed 2005; 400+ acres); hike-to Imperial Bowl / Lake Chutes toward the 12,998 ft summit; vertical 3,398 ft (1,036 m)","~355 in (~9 m) average annual snowfall (dry continental Colorado powder); snowmaking ~600 ac; longest run ''Four O''Clock'' ~3.5 mi; no night skiing; season early Nov into May (one of CO''s longest)","Base elevation ~9,600 ft (town centre ~9,728 ft) - one of the highest ski towns in North America","Historic District ~250 preserved structures; founded 1859 on the Blue River gold rush (town incorporated 1880); free BreckConnect gondola (town to Peak 7/8, opened 2006)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: #1 or #2 most-visited US resort (~1.5M/yr), swaps with Vail; published traffic where available (Breck #1/Vail #2, Vail Resorts disclosure) + industry consensus - never a hard live figure","Epic Pass (~$1,051-1,075 launch, dynamic); window single-day ~$179-269, Epic Day ~$47-100/day - pass/package is the value, not the window ticket","DEN gateway ~102 mi via I-70 (~2-2.5 hr, 3+ in storms); Epic Mountain Express shuttle; St. Anthony Summit Hospital, Frisco (~9 mi, Level III trauma, Flight for Life)","Festivals: Ullr Fest + International Snow Sculpture Championships (Jan); Breck Epic 6-day MTB (~Aug) in green season","NO natural hot springs in Breckenridge (nearest 60-96 mi); NO dedicated lift-served cat-skiing (scenic snowcat only); Dew Tour heritage (not current elite-training)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain; Summit County Rescue Group + Flight for Life air evac","hospital":"St. Anthony Summit Hospital, Frisco (~9 mi) - Level III trauma, Flight for Life base; backcountry casualties airlifted","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~9,600 ft, summit 12,998 ft - AMS real; acclimatize, hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if worsening, HAPE/HACE call 911); AVALANCHE backcountry/sidecountry - CAIC ''Vail & Summit County'' zone daily bulletin (by ~4:30 PM), beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; tree-wells/deep-snow suffocation; cold + intense UV; I-70 winter driving + Colorado Traction Law (Sept 1-May 31, Dotsero-Morrison), escalates to Chain Law - check CDOT cotrip.org","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'', Feb-Mar) ski + Ullr Fest + Snow Sculpture (Jan) + spring break (Mar); Jul-Aug summer","shoulder":"early season (early Nov-mid Dec), Jan midweek, April spring skiing, Sep-early Oct","green":"May + late Oct-early Nov (mud months - resort closed/winding down, lowest rates)","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + ski-in/out condos 4-8 mo; Feb-Mar 3-6 mo; summer 2-4 mo; shoulder/April 2-6 wk; Epic Pass by early fall","off_season_specials":"April spring-skiing + festival packages; May/Nov value; summer hiking + alpine coaster + Breck Epic; Historic District year-round hook","event_peaks":"Ullr Fest (mid-winter), International Snow Sculpture Championships (late Jan), Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break, closing (Apr-May), Fourth